  "name": "Unsolved Problems Mega-Atlas",
  "alternateName": "Unsolved Problems Mega-Atlas V2.9.0",
  "description": "Deduplicated cross-disciplinary dataset of 2,000 unsolved, open, and hard problems across 8 Macro-Pillars, 28 Superdomains, 8 Physical/Formal Substrates, and 7 Abstraction Layers, wired into a 6,108-edge knowledge graph that Python/NetworkX audits as biconnected (0 articulation points, 0 dangling links), with 0thernes CSS & Titan Index rankings, gradients & margins, per-record epistemic verification flags, Nov 26, 2026 AI proof-claim audit & automated daily sync across 16 global registries + all 25 Left to Solve fronts (lefttosolve.com/programs), Hybrid RAG (100% MRR@5 on 25 benchmark queries), 12-tool MCP server, 3 finite Track B probes (LOG-002, NT-005, COMB-002), AutoResearch harness, and 103 audited zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 software-model invariant theorems (kernel-checked by Lean; 9 Palomar comparator targets accepted by six kernel checks across five distinct implementations). None of the 2,000 problems is solved by this work.",
  "version": "2.9.0",
  "datePublished": "2026-11-26",
  "url": "https://0thernes.github.io/unsolved-problems-mega-atlas/",
